WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
Close a switch.

2
00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:05.200
A battery starts to charge a
capacitor through a resistor.

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:10.430
Wait one time constant: the resistance
multiplied by the capacitance.

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.210
Big capacitor or small,
strong battery or weak,

5
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.610
the capacitor is always
about two-thirds full.

6
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.110
Not a half, not three-quarters.

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.730
Why that fraction, every time?

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.590
In this mission, you'll turn the loop
rule into a differential equation for the

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.510
charge on the capacitor.

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.940
Then you'll solve it, for
charging and for discharging,

11
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.210
and read what the solution tells you.

12
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.720
Your mission: find out where
the two-thirds comes from.
